.TH STARTUP-TIME 1 "November 2026" "startup-time-checker 1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
startup-time \- lock booting until a chosen time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B startup-time set
.I time
.br
.B startup-time get
.br
.B startup-time clear
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stores a time before which the machine refuses to finish booting. The check is
done early in boot by
.BR startup-time-check (8)
through
.IR startup-time-checker.service .
.PP
.I time
is anything
.BR date (1)
accepts with
.BR \-\-date ,
for example "tomorrow 07:00" or "now + 8 hours".
.PP
The program is setuid root. A non-root user may set a lock or move an active
lock later, but never earlier;
.B clear
requires root.
.SH FILES
.I /var/lib/startup-time.state
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR startup-time-check (8),
.BR date (1)
